-- Migration 016 (up): the boundaries a fresh workspace starts with.
--
-- The full COD-AB dataset is 456 MB and does not live in the repository, so a
-- fresh database used to have an empty region layer until somebody imported
-- it. This migration seeds the country outline and the 34 province outlines
-- instead, simplified to 0.05 degree: about 100 KB of SQL, enough for the map
-- to show Indonesia and for the drill-down to work.
--
-- The full dataset is still better. Import it with:
--
--   go run ./cmd/import-regions -file data/idn_admin_boundaries.geojson.zip -levels 0
--   go run ./cmd/import-regions -file data/idn_admin_boundaries.geojson.zip -levels 1
--
-- The importer replaces these rows with the exact boundaries, so seeding
-- first and importing later costs nothing.
--
-- Source: HDX dataset `cod-ab-idn` (Badan Pusat Statistik), licence CC BY-IGO.
--
-- Re-runnable: rows that already exist are left alone.


ON CONFLICT (level, code) DO NOTHING;